minixml: parseelt: stop at the end of the buffer after a namespace prefix

parseelt() skips the ':' of a prefixed element name and goes on reading
without checking for the end of the buffer, so input that ends in ':' inside
an element name reads one byte past the heap buffer.

Upstream commit 64ef08a12aabab57be0bf7e40f047c8f14dedf9c, made after
miniupnpc 2.3.3.

--- a/src/minixml.c
+++ b/src/minixml.c
@@ -145,6 +145,8 @@
 				{
 					i = 0;
 					elementname = ++p->xml;
+					if (p->xml >= p->xmlend)
+						return;
 				}
 			}
 			if(i>0)
